# Git delivery

## When to commit

- Commit **only when the user asks** or when `/ship-pr` / `/deliver-feature` Phase 6 runs with explicit ship intent.
- Do not commit proactively after routine edits.

## Before commit

Run in parallel: `git status`, `git diff`, `git log -5 --oneline`.

- Stage relevant files; never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials).
- Message: why > what; match repo style.
- Use HEREDOC for commit message; do not skip hooks.

## Amend

Use `git commit --amend` only when ALL apply: user requested amend, HEAD is yours unpushed, or hook auto-modified files after a successful commit you made. If commit failed or was pushed, create a **new** commit.

## Push and PR

- Push: `git push -u origin HEAD` when needed.
- **Never** force-push `main`/`master`.
- `gh pr create` / update PR **only after** `./tool/ci_verify.sh` exit 0.
- Do not push unless user asks or ship command/phase runs.

## Do not

- Update git config.
- Run destructive git commands (force push, hard reset) unless user explicitly orders.
- Use interactive git flags (`-i`).

Command detail: [`.cursor/commands/ship-pr.md`](../commands/ship-pr.md).
